Dear Team,

As we progress through Q4 of 2023, I wanted to provide an extensive overview of our current operations concerning drilling, refining, pipeline systems, exploration activities, and reserves management. This memo aims to highlight our position in the market, the challenges we face, and strategic initiatives underway to enhance our operational efficiency and sustainability.

### Drilling Operations

Our drilling operations are primarily concentrated in the Permian Basin, where we have successfully established a presence since 2015. Our subsidiary, Eagle Rock Drilling Co., has consistently delivered impressive results, with a drilling efficiency improvement of 15% over the past year. In 2022, we drilled 85 wells, achieving an average production rate of 1,200 barrels of oil equivalent per day (BOE/D) per well. This year, as of September, we have already surpassed 90 wells, and we project to reach a total of 120 by year-end.

Our partnership with Schlumberger for advanced drilling technology has played a pivotal role in this success. The use of their DrillPlan system has optimized our drilling programs, reducing drilling time by up to 20% and minimizing operational costs. The estimated savings from these efficiencies alone amount to approximately $12 million annually.

### Refining Operations

The CrudeStar Refinery, located in Baytown, Texas, remains a cornerstone of our operations. Boasting a capacity of 300,000 barrels per day, it processes a diverse slate of crude oils sourced from both domestic and international markets. In 2023, we have expanded our refining capabilities to include a new hydrocracking unit, which has increased our production of ultra-low sulfur diesel by 30%.

Furthermore, we are actively pursuing compliance with the latest Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) regulations regarding emissions. Our investment of $50 million in carbon capture technology, developed in collaboration with Carbon Clean Solutions, is expected to reduce our greenhouse gas emissions by 40% by 2025. 

### Pipeline Infrastructure

The transportation of crude oil and refined products is facilitated through our extensive pipeline network, which spans over 2,000 miles across Texas and New Mexico. Our strategic partnership with TransCanada has enabled the development of the Gulf Coast Pipeline, which has increased our transport capacity by 25% this year. We have successfully transported an average of 1 million barrels of crude oil daily through this network, connecting our drilling sites to the CrudeStar Refinery efficiently.

We are also exploring the integration of advanced monitoring systems, such as the Pipeline Integrity Management System (PIMS) developed by Siemens, which would enhance our ability to detect leaks and ensure safety along our pipelines. An investment of $15 million is earmarked for this initiative in 2024.

### Exploration Initiatives

Our exploration efforts have focused primarily on the offshore Gulf of Mexico, where we hold significant acreage in the Green Canyon area. Since acquiring the lease in 2020, we have conducted three seismic surveys, identifying promising structures believed to hold recoverable reserves of 150 million barrels of oil equivalent. 

In collaboration with our geological team led by Dr. Lisa Chen, we plan to initiate exploratory drilling in early 2024, targeting three key sites. The successful development of these reserves could potentially increase our annual production by 20% by 2025.

### Reserves Management

As of Q3 2023, our proven reserves stand at 1.2 billion barrels of oil equivalent, a 10% increase from the previous year, largely attributed to our successful drilling and exploration efforts. Our reserves are audited annually by Ryder Scott, ensuring compliance with SEC guidelines.

The relationship between our drilling activities and reserves management is crucial. Our reserve replacement ratio has improved to 150% this year, thanks to the integration of real-time data analytics through the Reserves Management System (RMS) developed by Halliburton. This system allows us to monitor production rates and make informed decisions about future drilling targets based on current performance metrics.

